{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 130, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 carries no signal, so a conv on edge 1->2 adds nothing useful, while with a live node 1 it adds a deeper conv path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a pooling op on the input-output shortcut for an identity restores a clean residual, which helps far more than swapping out a conv or none."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the identity residual from input to output hurts trainability more than removing a conv or pooling op on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op with a 3x3 conv adds the most capacity, whereas replacing a skip removes a useful shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge into the output adds a new learned path, which is more beneficial than replacing an existing skip connection."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting the input to node 1 is costly when node 1 feeds the output through a conv, but nearly free when node 1's outputs are unused."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading the final node-2 to output edge from pooling to conv adds the most capacity, relative to replacing skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With no direct input-output edge, removing edge 2->3 removes one of the few remaining paths to the output, so it hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an identity on the first edge with a 1x1 conv drops a shortcut that conv-light cells depend on, which hurts more than replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning a 3x3 conv into pooling on an output edge loses learned capacity, which hurts more than replacing a 1x1 conv, skip, or none."}], "tok": 17829, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_